# UxPlay defaults — Silver Goggles (KDE Wayland / Dell G15 5520, RTX 3060)
#
# Format: one option per line, WITHOUT the leading "-" of the command-line flag.
# Installed to ~/.config/uxplayrc by `ujust airplay-setup` (never overwritten).
# Full reference: `man uxplay` or `uxplay -h`.
#
# IMPORTANT: only lines whose FIRST character is "#" are comments. read_config_file()
# (uxplay.cpp) splits every other line into argv entries on whitespace, so a trailing
# "# ..." would be parsed as option arguments. Keep every comment on its own line.
#
# Any value containing a space MUST be quoted: the same splitter honours ' and " as
# item delimiters, but without them "n Silver Goggles" becomes three argv entries and
# uxplay dies with `unknown option Goggles`.

n "Silver Goggles"

# Do not append "@hostname" to the advertised name. Without this the iOS picker shows
# "Silver Goggles@bazzite.drake-ayu.ts.net".
nh

# Fixed "legacy" ports (TCP 7100,7000,7001 / UDP 6000,6001,7011). Without this,
# UxPlay picks ports at random, which no firewall rule can anticipate.
p

# Client authentication. "pin" shows a 4-digit code on the terminal for every new
# client; "reg" persists authenticated clients to ~/.uxplay.register so trusted
# devices are not re-prompted. Dropping both makes any host on the LAN able to
# mirror onto this screen unprompted.
pin
reg

# xvimagesink (via XWayland), NOT waylandsink — measured on this host, KDE Wayland
# + RTX 3060. All three were tried against the same iPhone:
#   * waylandsink  -> geometry correct, content shredded into displaced horizontal
#                     bands. GST_DEBUG=2 showed the cause: "<videodmabufpool0> no caps
#                     in config" (gstvideopool.c:226) — it negotiates a dmabuf pool
#                     with no caps, so the stride is wrong. Identical corruption with
#                     nvh264dec and with software avdec, and the log carried no decoder
#                     error at all, which is what rules the decoder out.
#   * glimagesink  -> window opens, renders nothing (solid black).
#   * xvimagesink  -> correct. System memory, no dmabuf negotiation.
# Re-test waylandsink after GStreamer updates; XWayland is a workaround, not a goal.
vs xvimagesink
as pipewiresink

# NVDEC h264 decoding on the RTX 3060, via the GStreamer "nvcodec" plugin
# (gstreamer1-plugins-bad-free + libcuda). Note that commenting this out does NOT get
# you software decoding: decodebin picks nvcodec on its own here (verified by
# libgstnvcodec.so + libnvcuvid.so being mapped into the process). Use the "avdec"
# option for a genuinely software path.
#
# nvcodec also logs "Could not open nvrtc library libnvrtc.so" on this image — the CUDA
# runtime compiler is not shipped, so its GPU colour-conversion kernels fall back. This
# is a warning, not the corruption cause: the shredded image reproduced identically
# under software decode. See the videosink comment above.
vd nvh264dec

# Inhibit the screensaver while UxPlay runs, over the org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
# D-Bus service. Upstream notes this may not take effect on Wayland.
scrsv 2

# Lift the default 30fps cap. Measured with "FPSdata" against an iPhone 13 on 5GHz
# Wi-Fi 6: the client then reports encoderCurrentFPS 60 with sinkOverflowDropFPS,
# encoderDropFPS, encoderQueueDropFPS and idleDropFPS ALL zero, lossAvg 0.0006,
# rttAvg 3-5ms, and txUsageAvg ~0.6 MB/s against a txCapacityAvg of 8 MB/s — i.e. it
# costs ~7% of the negotiated capacity. Before this, the server-side pipeline dropped
# roughly every other frame ("Dropping frame due to QoS" from the videodecoder), which
# is what the 30fps default buys you on a link with headroom.
fps 60

# Audio latency reported to the client: 0.25s default -> 0.1s.
al 0.1

# Uncomment for pure screen mirroring (second-monitor / webcam use): drops
# timestamp-based A/V sync for lower latency. Deliberately left commented: it was tried
# here and the UI felt fine, but "fine" was judged on interactive content, never against
# a talking head — and giving up timestamp sync is exactly what drifts lip sync on video
# playback. Opt in per use, do not make it the default on the strength of an untested
# case.
# vsync no
